# Enemy_BombDropper_DropBomb: the bomb not spawned (ruling 5, 2), at its first call: the object
# pool has no free block (g_ObjPoolFree = 0), so Enemy_BouncingBomb_Spawn fails and the native
# drops its saved d0/a0 and returns -1. A full pool is a state the game handles; the corpus never
# fills it.

case pool_empty
b $FFFFF4B0 = 0
